@meta
id: 04-11
title: Drill — four lines, one typing
chapter: 04
type: drill
skills: count-prefix
par: 30
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: type it, copy it, paste it three times
open: review.md

@brief
Eight times: add four identical `- [ ] follow up` lines to the end of the
file, typing the text once. Save, quit, repeat.

@keys
| `4o` | open four lines below, repeating what you type |
| `5j` | down five lines |

@hints
The count goes in front of `o`.
--
Nothing appears four times until you press `Esc`. Trust it and leave
insert mode.

@solution
    5j 4o - [ ] follow up <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Twenty-four keystrokes for four lines.

The rep you are building is the pause before the typing: hand goes to the
count *before* it goes to the command. New vim users type `o`, then the
text, then think "I need three more of those". By rep eight, the count
should arrive first, because after the fact it is no use to you.

@start review.md
# Sprint 42 review

## Shipped

- refund window
- webhook retries

@expected review.md
# Sprint 42 review

## Shipped

- refund window
- webhook retries
- [ ] follow up
- [ ] follow up
